From ba3f9cff96cffae6094fab9562ea8144a163f681 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:09:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] thingino-ipud: on-camera object detection on the
 Infinity6C IPU

ipud runs a compiled YOLOv5 model on the SoC's IPU. It takes frames from an
SCL output port raptor left unused, at the model's input size, into the
IPU's input tensor without a copy where the frame layout allows; runs the
model through the drop's libmi_ipu; decodes the boxes with per-class NMS;
and reports them to a status file (a web UI page and a preview overlay), a
UNIX socket (/run/ipud.sock, read with ipucat) and MQTT. S35ipud starts it
from the ipud block of /etc/thingino.json, and a raptor.d hook stops it
before rvd tears the pipeline down and starts it again after.

Every SigmaStar board ships it, off until enabled. The model and the IPU
firmware are vendor files and are not included: the model is read from the
image (when its build staged one), from a folder on the SD card, or from a
custom path. A report class the model lacks is skipped with a warning.
